    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311-a1">

                <pb facs="0720" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg672"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-14"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >February</hi> 14, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In consequence of the revolt of Tokugawa
                    Yoshinobu, Munragi No Miyra, a prince of the blood and of the second rank, has
                    been appointed conimander-in chief of the army of execution. The government of
                    the United States being neutral, it is not to be supposed that assistance of any
                    kind will be given to Tokugawa Yoshinobu, either by transporting his troops or
                    those of Daimios acting under his orders, or by importing arms or vessels of
                    war, or by lending the service of American officers or soldiers.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to propose to you that you should notify citizens of the United
                    States to this effect, and that your government should take measures in order to
                    the preservation of strict neutrality.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HIGASHI KUZA SAKI NO SHOSHO.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Van Vankenburgh</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">American Minister.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
